{"abstract":[{"text":"Writes or checks ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand\/trackingPlan","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" as the command’s arguments say, and exits.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"main"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Given one argument, a directory, it writes the plan there, as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/write(to:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does: it exits with status 0 once the plan is written, and 73 ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EX_CANTCREAT"},{"type":"text","text":") when a file"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can’t be written."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Given "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check"},{"type":"text","text":" and a directory, it compares the plan with the one committed there, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(againstDirectory:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" does, printing the check’s report when they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"differ: it exits with status 0 when they match, 1 when a difference is breaking, and 2 when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the committed plan is only out of date."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Given ","type":"text"},{"code":"check --breaking-only","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a directory, it compares them the same way but fails only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when a difference is breaking: it exits with status 1 then, printing the report, and 0 when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they match or the plan there is only out of date. It prints the differences of an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out-of-date plan to standard output, as information.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Given ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iglu"},{"text":", a vendor, the kind of registry (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"server"},{"text":" for Iglu Server, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static"},{"text":" for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"static repository) and a directory, it writes the plan’s events there as the schemas of an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Iglu registry under that vendor, as ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does: it exits with status 0 once they are written, 64 (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EX_USAGE"},{"text":") for a vendor Iglu","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t take, 65 (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EX_DATAERR"},{"text":") for an event the registry can’t hold (a name Iglu doesn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"take, a keyword Snowplow doesn’t support, a breaking change at a published version, or, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a static repository, any change at one), and 73 when a file can’t be read or written.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Given anything else, it exits with status 64 (","type":"text"},{"code":"EX_USAGE","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"): ","type":"text"},{"code":"check","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alone (write to ","type":"text"},{"code":".\/check","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for a directory of that name), ","type":"text"},{"code":"check --breaking-only","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alone, the flag in any other place,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"iglu","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" without a vendor, a kind and a directory, a kind other than ","type":"text"},{"code":"server","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"static","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directory or vendor whose name starts with ","type":"text"},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a mistyped option would (write ","type":"text"},{"code":".\/-name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for a directory). When ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand\/trackingPlan"},{"text":" throws, it exits with status 65 (","type":"text"},{"code":"EX_DATAERR","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"failure is printed to standard error.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand\/main()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand"]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:13TrackingPlans0A11PlanCommandPAAE4mainyyFZ","roleHeading":"Type Method","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"main","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"title":"main()","symbolKind"